Z||000002||TRiAD||12-16-2001||03:59 PM||||Well, I don't work for a "proving grounds", or a magazine (yet?), and I don't steal them... LOL!<P>TRiAD Motorsports has been producing and selling aftermarket bolt-on performance parts and accessories for over 7 years now, and in the last 3 years, has begun offering a "brokering" service, primarilly for exotics and ultra-rare collectibles. <P>I have "connections" in the exotic/supercar industry, as well with individuals and enthusiast groups, and they all contact me occasionally for my services.<P>They either have a vehicle they want appraised or sold/traded, or have found a vehicle they want to possibly buy. Depending on the size of the transaction, my fee is usually something around $1K + expenses (plane tickets, etc) to go personally appraise and evaluate a vehicle for them, and anywhere from 1-10% from each party, depending on the size of the transaction. Larger transactions (anything over about $250K) get the 1% deal. This is always paid by each party. Cars that only cost $25K (Lotus Esprits, older Ferraris, some collectibles) generally pay close to 10%, and occasionally this is paid by each side.<P>It has been REAL slow this year, but sometimes can be great. I hope to make this a permanent thing in the nearish future. <P>I do NOT "inventory" cars at this point, and if I ever do, it will be a maximum of 3 at a time, and nothing over $150K each. It's better to "broker" than to simply "sell". <P>Hope this answers your question...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAAAMsSN*Wryq60N*CeWB!hXjfeIaMEc1YxPH9aPzaIXm!17ZpdBFE0Yk*d*dHNFG*GR3SFyLa8KJgh1IKe2Q/xmas-sig.jpg">       <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="red">Merry Christmas!</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B><BR>Photoshop rendition of planned modifications<BR>AIM ~ Michael Blue 72</I></FONT>||||reg||6
Z||000003||artherd||12-17-2001||01:09 AM||||Hey Triad, nothing personal here, I'm just wondering why you can't afford to fix your Fiero if you're dealing with so many exotics all the time?<P>Just puzzling, maybe you need to increase your fees, charge what you're worth man  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Yes, 'this ecomoney' sucks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
